<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17792" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτο-λήκῠθος</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who carries his own
				oil-flask, one who has no slave to do so</i>: hence,
				<i>wretchedly poor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				105
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐ., οἱ,</span> 'the Beggars', name of a club, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				54.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>flatterer, parasite,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Lex.</u>
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.50c
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
